__pycache__/
*.so
*.o
*.mod
sem_2d_f90
matrices_p*.txt
.venv/
.venv.old-py39/

# numba compiled-kernel cache (per fastmath flavour)
__nbcache__/

# Simulation output: every run saves a uniquely-named .npz so results can be
# compared without re-solving, but they are working data (30 MB and growing),
# not artefacts.  Regenerate with the driver scripts.
#
# Frame dumps from long runs land in SUBDIRECTORIES, which `scratch/*.npz` does
# not match, so the nested pattern is separate.  It must be on its own line:
# .gitignore has no trailing-comment syntax, so `pattern  # note` is read as one
# literal pattern and silently matches nothing.  That is exactly what happened
# here -- the nested rule never fired, and 45 checkpoints from the Re=400 TGV run
# were sitting uncovered.
scratch/*.npz
scratch/**/*.npz
*.log

# Rendered frames and VTK exports from those same runs: regenerate from the npz.
scratch/**/png/
scratch/tgv_vtk_*/

# Third-party publications: fetch locally, never commit.  See reference/README.md
reference/*.pdf
